1
00:00:02,910 --> 00:00:06,380
Great. Great. Just give me a sec to change film.

2
00:00:06,670 --> 00:00:11,460
Okay. I know I'm not supposed to know, but I do and I am so excited for you.

3
00:00:11,760 --> 00:00:14,470
Why? What's going on?

4
00:00:11,760 --> 00:00:14,470
Monica's pregnant.

5
00:00:15,840 --> 00:00:19,140
Oh, my God! Is that why you guys had to get married?

6
00:00:19,350 --> 00:00:22,770
Guys, I'm not pregnant!

7
00:00:19,350 --> 00:00:22,770
Ah, slow swimmers?

8
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:28,440
What? What do you mean? You're not pregnant?

9
00:00:28,610 --> 00:00:32,190
You didn't tell anybody I was, did you?

10
00:00:28,610 --> 00:00:32,190
No.

11
00:00:32,900 --> 00:00:34,240
I'll be right back.

12
00:00:35,070 --> 00:00:37,870
Now why don't we get a shot of Monica and the bloody soldier?

13
00:00:38,070 --> 00:00:40,990
Oh, about that. Joey, you have to change before the party.

14
00:00:41,160 --> 00:00:43,000
I can't. I don't have any other clothes.

15
00:00:43,160 --> 00:00:47,830
Find some. Please! Anything that doesn't say, "I died tragically in France."

16
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:52,420
Then why don't we see the bride and the groom, and the bridesmaids?

17
00:00:53,760 --> 00:00:56,930
Hey, Mon? Why did you tell the guys that you weren't pregnant?

18
00:00:57,090 --> 00:00:58,180
Because I'm not.

19
00:00:58,390 --> 00:01:01,720
We found your test in the trash. If you're not pregnant...

20
00:01:06,390 --> 00:01:08,600
...it's because I am.

21
00:01:09,860 --> 00:01:11,980
What are you talking about?

22
00:01:12,150 --> 00:01:15,190
Yes. Ahem. I am with child.

23
00:01:16,950 --> 00:01:19,820
And I didn't wanna say anything because it's your day.

24
00:01:19,990 --> 00:01:23,410
I didn't wanna steal your thunder.

25
00:01:19,990 --> 00:01:23,410
So you told people I was pregnant?

26
00:01:24,120 --> 00:01:26,910
Does this look like a conversation I wanna remember?

27
00:01:28,080 --> 00:01:29,500
Who's the father?

28
00:01:28,080 --> 00:01:29,500
Yeah.

29
00:01:30,170 --> 00:01:31,540
I can't say.

30
00:01:32,130 --> 00:01:33,670
Why?

31
00:01:32,130 --> 00:01:33,670
Why not?

32
00:01:34,340 --> 00:01:37,590
I can't say because he's famous.

33
00:01:38,510 --> 00:01:40,180
Oh, my God, who is it?

34
00:01:41,970 --> 00:01:44,100
Come on, you have to tell us.

35
00:01:44,270 --> 00:01:47,680
Okay, okay. It's James Brolin.

36
00:01:49,020 --> 00:01:51,810
James Brolin is the father of my baby.

37
00:01:52,190 --> 00:01:55,070
As in, Barbra Streisand's husband, James Brolin?

38
00:01:55,780 --> 00:01:59,700
What? He never said that to me.

39
00:02:38,030 --> 00:02:41,280
Monica, if you can step away, we'll get Chandler and the bridesmaids.

40
00:02:41,450 --> 00:02:43,070
How about just the bridesmaids?

41
00:02:43,580 --> 00:02:46,030
I am the groom. I was told it was kind of a big deal.

42
00:02:46,370 --> 00:02:48,370
It is.

43
00:02:46,370 --> 00:02:48,370
Yeah.

44
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:52,580
Oh, my God!

45
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:52,580
Thank you for doing that.

46
00:02:52,750 --> 00:02:54,710
I just can't deal with this just quite yet.

47
00:02:54,880 --> 00:02:56,710
So instead you told me Monica was pregnant?     -

48
00:02:56,880 --> 00:02:58,710
You did, I just didn't disagree.

49
00:02:59,470 --> 00:03:01,300
Sneaky!

50
00:02:59,470 --> 00:03:01,300
Yeah.

51
00:03:01,760 --> 00:03:03,760
Smile, ladies!

52
00:03:01,760 --> 00:03:03,760
Ohh.

53
00:03:04,640 --> 00:03:07,850
By the way, James Brolin?

54
00:03:04,640 --> 00:03:07,850
Ugh. I know.

55
00:03:08,270 --> 00:03:12,060
I could only think of two names: Him and Ed Begley Jr. And then...

56
00:03:12,980 --> 00:03:15,810
I remembered he's gay, so...

57
00:03:16,320 --> 00:03:19,940
Ed Begley Jr. Is not gay.

58
00:03:16,320 --> 00:03:19,940
Really?

59
00:03:29,790 --> 00:03:33,460
Thank you very much. Ladies and gentlemen, it gives me great pleasure...

60
00:03:33,630 --> 00:03:35,580
...to introduce to you for the first time:

61
00:03:35,750 --> 00:03:38,750
Mr. And Mrs. Chandler Bing!

62
00:03:44,260 --> 00:03:46,450
Before we go out there, I got a present for you.

63
00:03:46,660 --> 00:03:49,180
I'm not gonna put my hand in your pocket.

64
00:03:49,390 --> 00:03:50,810
No.

65
00:03:49,390 --> 00:03:50,810
No?

66
00:03:50,980 --> 00:03:52,980
I've been taking dancing lessons.

67
00:03:50,980 --> 00:03:52,980
What?

68
00:03:53,190 --> 00:03:56,730
Yeah, for the last 6 weeks. I wanted this to be a moment you'd never forget.

69
00:03:56,940 --> 00:03:58,900
Aww. That is so sweet!

70
00:03:59,190 --> 00:04:02,610
So would you care to join me in our first dance as husband and wife?

71
00:04:02,950 --> 00:04:04,910
Yes.

72
00:04:02,950 --> 00:04:04,910
Okay.

73
00:04:08,660 --> 00:04:12,500
What's the matter?

74
00:04:08,660 --> 00:04:12,500
These new shoes are all slippery.

75
00:04:12,710 --> 00:04:15,790
Are you going to be able to do this?

76
00:04:12,710 --> 00:04:15,790
Not well.

77
00:04:22,260 --> 00:04:25,680
Well, the good news is I don't think anyone's looking at us.

78
00:04:26,720 --> 00:04:30,890
So you ready to talk about it?

79
00:04:26,720 --> 00:04:30,890
No.

80
00:04:32,850 --> 00:04:34,390
Now?

81
00:04:35,730 --> 00:04:37,560
No.

82
00:04:37,730 --> 00:04:39,690
Okay, we'll talk about something else.

83
00:04:39,860 --> 00:04:41,320
Thank you.

84
00:04:39,860 --> 00:04:41,320
Who's the father?

85
00:04:41,480 --> 00:04:44,740
Uh. Look, honey, I haven't told him yet...

86
00:04:44,900 --> 00:04:47,950
...so until I do, I don't think I should tell anybody else.

87
00:04:48,120 --> 00:04:52,080
Yeah. That's fine. That's fair. Is it Tag?

88
00:04:52,250 --> 00:04:53,660
Ugh. Phoebe!

89
00:04:53,830 --> 00:04:55,750
Okay. I'm sorry, I'll stop.

90
00:04:53,830 --> 00:04:55,750
Okay.

91
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:57,460
Is it Ross? It's Ross, isn't it?

92
00:04:57,670 --> 00:05:00,540
Oh, my God, it's Joey!

93
00:04:57,670 --> 00:05:00,540
Honey, stop it, okay?

94
00:05:00,750 --> 00:05:02,750
I'm not going to tell you until I tell him.

95
00:05:02,920 --> 00:05:05,800
Ah-ha! At least we know it's a him.

96
00:05:11,930 --> 00:05:13,970
Oh, sweet lord.

97
00:05:14,140 --> 00:05:15,180
I'm sorry, okay?

98
00:05:15,390 --> 00:05:18,730
I went down to the gift shop, and it was either this or a bathrobe.

99
00:05:18,900 --> 00:05:22,520
Look, what's more important? The way I'm dressed or me being with you today?

100
00:05:22,690 --> 00:05:26,570
Honey, I'm not even going to pretend I was listening. Hey! Hey.

101
00:05:32,240 --> 00:05:33,540
Hi.

102
00:05:33,750 --> 00:05:37,660
I'm Ross. I don't believe we've met. I'm Monica's older brother.

103
00:05:37,870 --> 00:05:41,380
Hi, I'm Mona from her restaurant.

104
00:05:37,870 --> 00:05:41,380
Oh.

105
00:05:41,590 --> 00:05:44,880
Hello, "Mona from her restaurant."

106
00:05:49,180 --> 00:05:51,890
Mona. What a beautiful name.

107
00:05:52,060 --> 00:05:54,560
You think so? I always kind of hated it.

108
00:05:55,020 --> 00:05:57,140
Aw, come on! Mona Lisa?

109
00:05:55,020 --> 00:05:57,140
Uh-huh.

110
00:05:57,350 --> 00:05:59,770
Mona...

111
00:05:59,980 --> 00:06:01,610
...Klegglachen?

112
00:06:02,900 --> 00:06:05,230
The famous botanist. Huh?

113
00:06:05,440 --> 00:06:08,860
Oh, no. She's... Well, she's dead now.

114
00:06:09,070 --> 00:06:13,990
But supposedly she was once quite the hottie of the plant world.

115
00:06:14,410 --> 00:06:15,700
Really?

116
00:06:14,410 --> 00:06:15,700
Yeah.

117
00:06:15,870 --> 00:06:20,580
Well, see, I never knew about her.

118
00:06:15,870 --> 00:06:20,580
Linda Klegglachen...

119
00:06:24,090 --> 00:06:26,420
So, what table are you at?

120
00:06:27,170 --> 00:06:29,550
Oh, heh, me too.

121
00:06:29,880 --> 00:06:32,800
Good. There will be someone who likes my name.

122
00:06:33,050 --> 00:06:34,850
Yes, there will.

123
00:06:41,520 --> 00:06:46,730
Guess what, Molly Gilbert. You've just been bumped up to table one.

124
00:06:46,940 --> 00:06:51,660
And if it's all right with you, I'm gonna take your place at table six.

125
00:06:51,860 --> 00:06:54,320
Martin Klegglachen!

126
00:06:55,950 --> 00:07:01,370
That's better. Just bend your arms a little more. There you go. Look straight ahead.

127
00:07:01,540 --> 00:07:04,330
Now this time I want you to really put your ass into it.

128
00:07:07,510 --> 00:07:09,540
Chandler, darling, look, my date has finally arrived.

129
00:07:09,710 --> 00:07:12,840
I'd like you to meet Dennis Phillips.

130
00:07:13,050 --> 00:07:15,180
Congratulations.

131
00:07:13,050 --> 00:07:15,180
Thanks.

132
00:07:15,390 --> 00:07:19,020
Dennis is a dear old friend. And a fantastic lover.

133
00:07:19,230 --> 00:07:23,230
Bravo, Dennis, thanks for pleasing my mother so.

134
00:07:24,310 --> 00:07:27,980
I'm so sorry I missed the ceremony. I was stuck at auditions.

135
00:07:28,190 --> 00:07:30,570
Dennis is directing a new Broadway show.

136
00:07:30,740 --> 00:07:33,030
Hi, I don't believe we've met. Joey Tribbiani.

137
00:07:33,200 --> 00:07:36,240
Dennis Phillips.

138
00:07:33,200 --> 00:07:36,240
Wow. I've admired your work for years.

139
00:07:36,410 --> 00:07:37,910
You've done some amazing stuff.

140
00:07:38,200 --> 00:07:41,330
Thank you. Excuse me, I'll get myself a drink.

141
00:07:41,540 --> 00:07:43,330
I'll be back in a moment.

142
00:07:43,580 --> 00:07:46,670
Dennis Phillips! That's great! How did you guys meet?

143
00:07:46,840 --> 00:07:48,500
Well, you know, it's a funny story.

144
00:07:48,710 --> 00:07:51,590
Funny "ha-ha," or funny "boom, uh-oh!"

145
00:08:00,020 --> 00:08:03,090
Thank you very much. Now if everyone will please take their seats,

146
00:08:03,220 --> 00:08:04,390
dinner will be served.

147
00:08:14,820 --> 00:08:15,860
Hey.

148
00:08:16,120 --> 00:08:21,330
Uh, I thought you were at table six.

149
00:08:16,120 --> 00:08:21,330
Uh, no. Nine.

150
00:08:23,210 --> 00:08:27,960
Ohh. See, before, when you showed it to me, you held it that way...

151
00:08:28,170 --> 00:08:32,050
...which was misleading.

152
00:08:34,380 --> 00:08:36,470
Well... I'll... um...

153
00:08:43,100 --> 00:08:44,390
Hello.

154
00:08:50,940 --> 00:08:55,200
Chandler! Will you see if your mom can give my resume to Dennis Phillips?

155
00:08:55,400 --> 00:08:58,620
Because if I can get into a Broadway show, I would've done it all:

156
00:08:58,780 --> 00:09:00,120
Film, television and theater.

157
00:09:00,280 --> 00:09:03,580
The only thing left would be radio, and that's just for ugly people.

158
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:08,420
What size shoes do you wear?

159
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:08,420
Uh, eleven. Eleven and a half.

160
00:09:08,580 --> 00:09:11,290
Great. My shoes are giving me a problem on the dance floor.

161
00:09:11,460 --> 00:09:13,570
Can I borrow the boots from your costume?

162
00:09:13,760 --> 00:09:16,970
I don't know where I left those, so...

163
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:21,890
Those aren't eleven and a half.

164
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:21,890
Okay, fine, I'm a 7!

165
00:09:22,100 --> 00:09:26,060
All right, I have surprisingly small feet. But the rest of me is good! I'll show you!

166
00:09:28,980 --> 00:09:33,610
Can you believe Phoebe got pregnant?

167
00:09:28,980 --> 00:09:33,610
Let's not talk about that now.

168
00:09:33,820 --> 00:09:37,700
This is so huge.

169
00:09:33,820 --> 00:09:37,700
Sure, but as big as your wedding?

170
00:09:37,910 --> 00:09:40,160
Of course not. Nothing is.

171
00:09:40,870 --> 00:09:42,910
Wow. Between me and you?

172
00:09:40,870 --> 00:09:42,910
Yeah.

173
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:46,500
In this day and age, how dumb do you have to be to get pregnant?

174
00:09:46,660 --> 00:09:50,830
Hey, sometimes you can do everything right, wear what you're supposed to...

175
00:09:51,040 --> 00:09:53,710
...and one of those little guys just gets through.

176
00:09:54,880 --> 00:09:58,090
How?

177
00:09:54,880 --> 00:09:58,090
I don't know, maybe they have tools.

178
00:09:59,470 --> 00:10:03,010
Well, I talked to her, and she's definitely gonna have this baby.

179
00:10:03,180 --> 00:10:06,100
She's gonna raise it on her own.

180
00:10:06,560 --> 00:10:09,690
Well, maybe that's really brave.

181
00:10:06,560 --> 00:10:09,690
Maybe.

182
00:10:09,850 --> 00:10:12,520
I just hope she realizes how hard it's gonna be.

183
00:10:15,150 --> 00:10:18,110
Maybe she hasn't really thought it through that much.

184
00:10:19,490 --> 00:10:21,360
There's a lot to think about.

185
00:10:21,530 --> 00:10:26,290
How is she gonna handle this financially? How is she gonna juggle work?

186
00:10:27,040 --> 00:10:31,210
Does she realize she's not gonna have a date again for the next 18 years?

187
00:10:35,210 --> 00:10:37,090
I don't know.

188
00:10:38,840 --> 00:10:40,470
Are you okay?

189
00:10:40,680 --> 00:10:41,930
Mm-hm.

190
00:10:42,300 --> 00:10:46,680
I'm just thinking about Phoebe. Poor, knocked-up Phoebe.

191
00:10:47,810 --> 00:10:51,480
Champagne?

192
00:10:47,810 --> 00:10:51,480
Oh, yes. Thank you very much. Whew.

193
00:11:04,700 --> 00:11:07,450
That's actually how the French drink it.

194
00:11:13,290 --> 00:11:17,920
Well, I just got off the phone with my lover, James Brolin.

195
00:11:19,760 --> 00:11:20,760
Really?

196
00:11:19,760 --> 00:11:20,760
Yes.

197
00:11:20,930 --> 00:11:23,260
And apparently, he is married to some singer.

198
00:11:25,300 --> 00:11:30,270
But he said he'd leave her for me. So I said, "Are you sure?"

199
00:11:30,430 --> 00:11:33,100
And James Brolin said...

200
00:11:30,430 --> 00:11:33,100
Rachel's the one who's pregnant?

201
00:11:33,270 --> 00:11:34,810
What?

202
00:11:36,860 --> 00:11:38,440
Why bother?

203
00:11:39,650 --> 00:11:41,280
How do you feel?

204
00:11:41,450 --> 00:11:43,990
I don't know how I feel. This is all happening so fast.

205
00:11:44,200 --> 00:11:47,280
I have to make all these decisions that I don't want to make.

206
00:11:47,450 --> 00:11:50,040
Mm! Oh! Someone take this away from me!

207
00:11:50,500 --> 00:11:53,790
Calm down. Maybe you're not pregnant.

208
00:11:50,500 --> 00:11:53,790
What?

209
00:11:54,040 --> 00:11:58,130
When I got pregnant with the triplets, I took the test three times.

210
00:11:58,340 --> 00:12:03,010
Yes. Maybe it's a false-positive. Are you sure you peed on the stick right?

211
00:12:03,430 --> 00:12:05,300
How many ways are there to do that?

212
00:12:06,260 --> 00:12:09,560
I'm just saying, don't freak out until you're 100 percent sure.

213
00:12:10,980 --> 00:12:12,980
I'll take it again at home.

214
00:12:13,230 --> 00:12:16,060
You gotta take it now, as a present to me.

215
00:12:17,730 --> 00:12:19,020
Okay. Thank you.

216
00:12:19,230 --> 00:12:22,240
I'll run out and get you one.

217
00:12:19,230 --> 00:12:22,240
Aw, you girls are so great.

218
00:12:22,650 --> 00:12:24,490
Wait a minute. Who's the father?

219
00:12:24,820 --> 00:12:27,620
She won't tell us.

220
00:12:24,820 --> 00:12:27,620
Come on! It's my wedding.

221
00:12:27,780 --> 00:12:29,120
That could be my present.

222
00:12:29,290 --> 00:12:34,000
Hey! I just gave you peeing on a stick.

223
00:12:29,290 --> 00:12:34,000
See, this is why you register.

224
00:12:40,840 --> 00:12:45,430
It was the chair again, okay? I'm not doing it!

225
00:12:45,680 --> 00:12:48,090
It was... Look, I don't. You know what?

226
00:12:52,310 --> 00:12:54,100
Hi.

227
00:12:52,310 --> 00:12:54,100
Hi.

228
00:12:54,350 --> 00:12:56,520
Would you like to dance?

229
00:12:54,350 --> 00:12:56,520
Sure.

230
00:12:56,690 --> 00:12:58,060
Yeah.

231
00:12:56,690 --> 00:12:58,060
Oh, great.

232
00:12:59,190 --> 00:13:02,360
Dr. Geller?

233
00:12:59,190 --> 00:13:02,360
I wasn't farting!

234
00:13:05,700 --> 00:13:08,530
Uh, a little game from our table.

235
00:13:09,370 --> 00:13:12,330
Yes?

236
00:13:09,370 --> 00:13:12,330
Dr. Geller, will you dance with me?

237
00:13:12,620 --> 00:13:14,540
Oh. Um...

238
00:13:15,210 --> 00:13:18,790
Maybe later. I'm about to dance with this lady.

239
00:13:19,340 --> 00:13:20,790
Okay.

240
00:13:21,300 --> 00:13:23,130
Ooooh.

241
00:13:23,460 --> 00:13:28,430
Unless this lady wouldn't mind letting you go first.

242
00:13:28,590 --> 00:13:31,470
I'd be happy to. You are very sweet.

243
00:13:31,640 --> 00:13:34,720
Ohh. Yes, I am.

244
00:13:35,850 --> 00:13:39,980
In fact, why don't we try it my special way. You can dance on my feet.

245
00:13:40,150 --> 00:13:42,190
Sure.

246
00:13:40,150 --> 00:13:42,190
Yeah? Hop on.

247
00:13:46,990 --> 00:13:49,490
Is the pretty lady looking?

248
00:13:46,990 --> 00:13:49,490
Uh-huh.

249
00:13:49,990 --> 00:13:51,910
Keep dancing.

250
00:14:02,750 --> 00:14:05,420
And the world will never know.

251
00:14:06,300 --> 00:14:10,300
Hey! Did you talk to Dennis?

252
00:14:06,300 --> 00:14:10,300
Yes. I told him how talented you were.

253
00:14:10,510 --> 00:14:12,000
I told him all about Days ofour Lives.

254
00:14:12,210 --> 00:14:15,600
No, you don't tell a Broadway guy that!

255
00:14:15,770 --> 00:14:19,940
Now he thinks I'm just a soap actor.

256
00:14:15,770 --> 00:14:19,940
But you're not just a soap actor.

257
00:14:20,100 --> 00:14:22,610
You are a soap actor with freakishly tiny feet.

258
00:14:22,770 --> 00:14:24,190
Hey.

259
00:14:33,280 --> 00:14:35,580
Thank you.

260
00:14:33,280 --> 00:14:35,580
No, thank you, Miranda.

261
00:14:35,740 --> 00:14:38,120
Melinda.

262
00:14:35,740 --> 00:14:38,120
All right.

263
00:14:38,460 --> 00:14:43,000
How cute was that?

264
00:14:38,460 --> 00:14:43,000
Oh! Were you watching?

265
00:14:44,750 --> 00:14:47,340
Can I go next?

